  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Record warmth possible Thursday.\n\nUpper level ridging will start to build tomorrow with above\nnormal temperatures returning (mid to upper 60s). Low level\nthicknesses build even further Thursday ahead of the next\nfrontal system, with widespread highs in the upper 60s to low\n70s expected. Some records will be threatened or broken with \nany additional heating into the mid 70s, which will be possible,\nespecially over the Genesee Valley due to downslope flow and \ndry soils (see Climate section below). A strengthening SW breeze\nmay cap heating along the eastern Lakeshores in the afternoon. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Abnormally dry conditions continue through the \nweekend. Brief shot of light rain Thursday night.\n\nDry high pressure will remain over the area through Thursday\nbefore a weak cold front moves through the region overnight and\nprovides chances for light rain showers. Very limited forcing\nwith this front will allow for only a few hundredths of an inch\nof rain to fall across most of Western and Central NY\nunfortunately. This will prolong our dry stretch of weather, \nwith some fire weather concerns due to the dryness of fuels and\nleaf litter. Luckily, winds and RH levels won't reach close to \ncritical levels through the weekend. See Fire weather section \nbelow for more details. High pressure builds back over the Great\nLakes Friday and into this weekend, with dry weather continuing\nuntil perhaps late Sunday.",
